{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1080 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b1b9f99300641e03e7cc7fb244879705309364881a9da82fa5c38618e4deabbd" :edb/db-before-t 1079 :edb/db-after-t 1080 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534392 50 #inst "2026-10-06T23:52:10.034Z" 13194139534392 true] [17592186119433 1100 "If $x=2y^2 + \\dfrac1{y^2}$, then find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}$." 13194139534392 false] [17592186119433 1100 "If $x=2y^2 + \\dfrac1{y^2}$, then find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}.$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186119433 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dy} &= \\frac{d}{dy}(2y^{2} + \\frac{1}{y^{2}}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dy}(2y^{2} + y^{-2}) \\\\\n&= 2\\frac{d}{dy}(y^{2}) + \\frac{d}{dy}(y^{-2}) \\\\\n&= 4y - 2y^{-3} \\\\\n&= 4y - \\frac{2}{y^{3}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4y^{4} - 2}{y^{3}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{y^3}{4y^4 -2}\n$$" 13194139534392 false] [17592186119433 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =4y-2{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =4y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{4}-2}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{y^3}{4y^4 -2}.\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186119434 1100 "If $x = y + 2y\\sqrt y$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}$ at the point $\\left(3 , 1\\right).$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186119434 1100 "If $x = y + 2y\\sqrt y$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}$ at the point $\\left(3, 1\\right)$." 13194139534392 false] [17592186119434 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dy} &= \\frac{d}{dy}(y + 2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dy}(y + 2y^{3/2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dy}(y) + 2\\frac{d}{dy}(y^{3/2}) \\\\\n&= 1 + 2 \\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}y^{1/2}) \\\\\n&= 1 + 3y^{1/2} \\\\\n&= 1 + 3\\sqrt{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{1 + 3\\sqrt y}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,1)$, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(x, y) = (3, 1)} &= \\frac{1}{1 + 3\\sqrt{1}} = \\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 false] [17592186119434 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =1+2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =1+3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =1+3\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} =  \\dfrac{1}{1 + 3\\sqrt y}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,1)} & =\\frac{1}{1+3\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186119435 1100 "What is the equation of the tangent to the curve $x = 2y^2 -y + 1$ at the point $(2,1)$?" 13194139534392 false] [17592186119435 1100 "What is the equation of the tangent to the curve $x = 2y^2 -y + 1$ at the point $(2,1)?$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186119435 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dy} &= \\frac{d}{dy}(2y^{2} - y + 1) \\\\\n&= 2\\frac{d}{dy}(y^{2}) - \\frac{d}{dy}(y) + \\frac{d}{dy}(1) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot (2y) - 1 + 0 \\\\\n&= 4y - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac1{4y - 1}\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(x, y) = (2, 1)} \\\\\n&= (1)/(4(1) - 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 1 &= \\frac{1}{3}(x - 2) \\\\\ny &= \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{2}{3} + 1 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{x}{3} + \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 false] [17592186119435 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}-y+1) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2y)-1+0 \\\\  & =4y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac1{4y - 1}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(2,1)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(2,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4(1)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186119860 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285861 13194139534392 true] [17592186119860 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285875 13194139534392 true] [17592186119860 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285903 13194139534392 true] [17592186119860 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285913 13194139534392 true] [17592186119861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285882 13194139534392 true] [17592186119861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285916 13194139534392 true] [17592186119861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285919 13194139534392 true] [17592186119861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285925 13194139534392 true] [17592186119862 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285868 13194139534392 true] [17592186119862 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285889 13194139534392 true] [17592186119862 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285896 13194139534392 true] [17592186119862 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285922 13194139534392 true] [17592186120126 1017 #edb/ref 17592186117276 13194139534392 false] [17592186120126 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285907 13194139534392 true] [17592186120126 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534392 true] [17592186120126 1100 "If $x = 2\\sqrt{y} - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $(5, 9)$." 13194139534392 false] [17592186120126 1100 "If $x=2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(5,9).$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186120126 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{y})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{1/2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-3/2}) \\\\  & ={y}^{-1/2}+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2y\\sqrt{y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y+3}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{2y\\sqrt{y}}{2y+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(5,9),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(5,9)} & =\\frac{2(9)\\sqrt{9}}{2(9)+3}=\\frac{18}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186120127 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534392 true] [17592186120127 1100 "Given a curve $x = \\frac{2}{3}y^{3} - y^{2}$, what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9, 3)$?" 13194139534392 false] [17592186120127 1100 "Given a curve $x=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)?$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186120127 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{y}^{2}-2y \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2{y}^{2}-2y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(9,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(3)^{2}-2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{12}(x-9) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}-\\frac{3}{4}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186120133 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534392 true] [17592186120133 1100 "If $x =-\\frac{2}{y^{2}} + 2y^{2}$, then $\\frac{dy}{dx} =$" 13194139534392 false] [17592186120133 1100 "If $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186120133 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-2}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4{y}^{-3}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}.\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285861 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285862 13194139534392 true] [17592186285861 1089 "q-109156" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285861 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534392 true] [17592186285861 1100 "If $x=5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285861 1113 #uuid "d402a78d-7baa-5a8f-a1ce-6df24cc00d98" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285861 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-10\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-20y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}.\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285863 13194139534392 true] [17592186285862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285864 13194139534392 true] [17592186285862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285865 13194139534392 true] [17592186285862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285866 13194139534392 true] [17592186285862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285867 13194139534392 true] [17592186285862 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534392 true] [17592186285862 1041 "selection" 13194139534392 true] 