17592186285913 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285914 13194139534392 true] [17592186285913 1089 "q-341608" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285913 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534392 true] [17592186285913 1100 "Given that $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | ${y}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285913 1113 #uuid "05897e0d-06be-55d9-88a0-39032be05a4f" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285913 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-1}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(-2{y}^{-3})+5(2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+10y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+10{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+10{y}^{4}}.\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285915 13194139534392 true] [17592186285914 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534392 true] [17592186285914 1041 "field-1" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285914 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285915 13194139534392 true] [17592186285914 1110 #uuid "97d53035-97e0-582c-afb0-253e72579b34" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285915 1034 "4+10y^4" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534392 true] [17592186285915 1111 #uuid "c37f9256-da8a-5ba7-bd60-ed511c831190" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285916 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285917 13194139534392 true] [17592186285916 1089 "q-341636" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285916 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534392 true] [17592186285916 1100 "If $x=2{y}^{3}+{y}^{2},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(20,2).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(20,2)}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285916 1113 #uuid "1ddc71d8-aab5-5e88-9690-82c0e13ce162" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285916 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2(3{y}^{2})+2y \\\\  & =6{y}^{2}+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{6{y}^{2}+2y}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(20,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(20,2)} & =\\frac{1}{6({2}^{2})+2(2)}=\\frac{1}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285918 13194139534392 true] [17592186285917 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534392 true] [17592186285917 1041 "field-1" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285917 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285918 13194139534392 true] [17592186285917 1110 #uuid "0c11e239-c3af-5db3-a5b7-e9d39cb32a4b" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285918 1034 "\\frac{1}{28}" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285918 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534392 true] [17592186285918 1111 #uuid "5a567409-0509-531d-9d9e-e5a94596563b" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285919 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285920 13194139534392 true] [17592186285919 1089 "q-341757" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285919 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534392 true] [17592186285919 1100 "If $x=-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(-14,1).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285919 1113 #uuid "aada2aac-9808-566e-a932-6ee841bb6da4" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285919 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2y\\cdot {y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12(-\\frac{1}{2}){y}^{-3/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =6{y}^{-3/2}-3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{y\\sqrt{y}}-3\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-3{y}^{2}}{y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{y\\sqrt{y}}{6-3{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(-14,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)} & =\\frac{1\\sqrt{1}}{6-3(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285921 13194139534392 true] [17592186285920 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534392 true] [17592186285920 1041 "field-1" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285920 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285921 13194139534392 true] [17592186285920 1110 #uuid "5cd43bec-34df-53b7-b316-a53d2403a1e4" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285921 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534392 true] [17592186285921 1111 #uuid "e2f80c6c-fdf9-588b-b84f-6a0f3d1a089a" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285922 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285923 13194139534392 true] [17592186285922 1089 "q-342049" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285922 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534392 true] [17592186285922 1100 "Given a curve $x=2y-\\frac{6}{y},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,3)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285922 1113 #uuid "45e88e0a-eda2-5d07-9063-d301368f5fe4" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285922 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2y-\\frac{6}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2y-6{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2(1)-6(-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2+6{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}+6}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}+6}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2(3)^{2}+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot (x-4) \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{8}x-\\frac{3}{2}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285923 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285924 13194139534392 true] [17592186285923 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534392 true] [17592186285923 1041 "field-1" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285923 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285924 13194139534392 true] [17592186285923 1110 #uuid "610faf0f-7729-5522-893e-0781abd865f2" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285924 1034 "\\frac{3x}{8}+\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285924 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534392 true] [17592186285924 1111 #uuid "90531a37-fc9e-5c9f-a16f-88465b373949" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285925 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285926 13194139534392 true] [17592186285925 1089 "q-51336" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285925 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534392 true] [17592186285925 1100 "If $x=\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(3,2).$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285925 1113 #uuid "4928953b-0350-5f60-9789-334738000d33" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285925 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{-1}+8{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-{y}^{-2})+8\\cdot (-2{y}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-2{y}^{-2}-16{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2y-16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y+16}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2y+16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,2)} & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{2(2)+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285927 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285928 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285929 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285930 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285931 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1041 "selection" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285927 13194139534392 true] [17592186285926 1110 #uuid "6b4ee07f-34bd-5d6c-a0e6-0da499fa1149" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285927 1034 "-\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534392 true] [17592186285927 1111 #uuid "0e0f1a8c-0ef0-52c7-a098-fafd807d4a8a" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285928 1034 "-\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534392 true] [17592186285928 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1